Here is the English translation of the provided text: "How will your people be suffering, you snakes and hypocrites! You blind guides! You strain out a gnat but swallow a camel. You clean the outside of the cup and of the dish, but inside they are full of greed and self-indulgence. You blind Pharisee! First clean the inside of the cup and of the dish, so that the outside of it may become clean also. Woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! For you build the tombs of the prophets and adorn the monuments of the righteous. And you say, 'If we had lived in the days of our fathers, we would not have participated with them in the shedding of the blood of the prophets.' Thus you testify against yourselves that you are the sons of those who murdered the prophets. Fill up then the measure of your fathers. Serpents! Brood of vipers! How can you escape the damnation of hell? For I send you prophets, wise men, and scribes, some of whom you will kill and crucify, and some of whom you will scourge in your synagogues and persecute from city to city, so that on you may come all the righteous blood shed on the earth, from the blood of righteous Abel to the blood of Zechariah, the son of Barachiah, whom you murdered between the temple and the altar. Truly I say to you, all these things will come upon this generation. O Jerusalem, Jerusalem, the city that kills the prophets and stones those who are sent to her! How often I would have gathered your children together as a hen gathers her brood under her wings, but you were not willing! Behold, your house is left to you desolate. For I tell you, you will not see Me again until you say, 'Blessed is He who comes in the name of the Lord.' Then will I tell you that the kingdom of God is come nigh unto you. For behold, the days are coming, says the Lord, that I will raise up from David a righteous Branch, and a king shall reign and prosper, and shall execute judgment and justice in the land. In his days shall Judah prosper, and Israel shall dwell securely. And this is the name by which he will be called: THE LORD OUR RIGHTEOUSNESS.
<.>
"What a disaster you are, you teachers of the law and you Pharisees, you hypocrites! You come from everywhere to make a single convert, and you make them twice as much a child of hell as yourselves. No, even more than you."
"What a disaster is upon you, you who blind the people! You say, 'If someone swears by the temple, there is nothing wrong. But if he swears by the gold of the temple, he must fulfill his oath.'"
You are blind and stupid! What is more important? The gold? Or the temple that sanctifies the gold?
You say, "If someone swears by the altar, it means nothing; but if someone swears by the gift that is on it, they must do it."
O ye blind! What is more important: the gift or the altar which sanctifies the gift?
whoever swears by the temple, he is swearing by it and by everything that is in it.
And anyone who swears by the temple is swearing by it and by whoever dwells in it.
And whoever swears by the name of heaven, he swears by the name of God's throne and of the one who sits on it.
"What a terrible misfortune has befallen you, you teachers of the law and you Pharisees! You hypocrites! You give a tenth of your spices, such as mint, dill and cumin. But you do not practice the most important things in the law, such as justice, mercy and faithfulness. You should have practiced the most important things without neglecting the less important ones."
O blind guides! You strain out the gnat of the least detail in your food, but you swallow the camel of the most essential principles!
"What a disaster this misfortune is upon you, you teachers of the law and you Pharisees! You hypocrites! You wash the outside of the cup and the plate. But inside, you are full of greed. You love to be greeted with honor and to have people call you 'Rabbi.' "
You blind Pharisee! Clean the inside of the cup and dish first. Then, the outside will become clean as well.
"What a disaster is upon you, you teachers of the law and you Pharisees! You hypocrites! You are like tombs that appear beautiful on the outside, adorned with white, but inside they are full of the bones of the dead. And there are other unclean and impure things within."
However you are. From the outside there is only work, but from the inside it is full of what is not right. Lies to yourself.
"What a disaster is upon you, O scribes and Pharisees, you hypocrites! You build the tombs of the prophets and decorate the tombs of the righteous."
And you say, "If we had lived in the time of those who came before us, we would not have done what they did. We would not have helped in the killing of the prophets."
You are the ones who bear witness against yourselves that you are the sons of those who murdered the prophets.
Complete the sins that those before you started for you!
"O nest of poisonous vipers! How will you escape being sentenced to fire?"
I will send you my prophets and wise men and teachers. You will kill some of them. You will crucify some of them on a cross. Some of them you will flog in your synagogue. You will expel some of them from city to city.
You will pay with the blood of every single righteous person you have shed on earth. From the blood of righteous Abel to the blood of Zechariah son of Berekiah. Zechariah whom you killed between the temple and the altar.
What I am going to tell you is true. This is going to happen to the people who are alive now.
Jerusalem! Jerusalem! You are killing the prophets and throwing stones to kill those whom God has sent to you. I have often wanted to gather you and embrace you, like a hen gathering her chicks under her wings. But you would not let me do that!
Look, your house is empty.
I tell you, you will not see me until you say, "Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord."
Signs of the Hour
